---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Risks & Realities" description="Safety data, risk disclosure, and honest assessment of what's dangerous, what's uncertain, and what we're doing about it.">

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="relative min-h-[40vh] flex items-end pb-12 overflow-hidden">
    <img src="/images/yungas/death-road.jpg" alt="The famous Death Road winding through the Yungas mountains" class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover" />
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-black/80 via-black/40 to-black/20"></div>
    <div class="relative z-10 max-w-[1400px] mx-auto px-6 lg:px-10 w-full">
      <span class="text-label text-accent">Honest Assessment</span>
      <h1 class="text-headline text-white mt-2">Risks & Realities</h1>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-bark-200 mt-2 max-w-xl">What's dangerous, what's uncertain, and what we're doing about it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Photo break -->
  <div class="photo-frame h-48 md:h-64 reveal">
    <img src="/images/yungas/road-panorama.jpg" alt="Panoramic view of the Yungas road" loading="lazy" class="w-full h-full object-cover" />
    <div class="photo-credit">The road is both the connection and the risk</div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================
       PART 1: LOCATION SAFETY
       ============================================ -->

  <!-- Crime Data -->
  <section class="py-24 px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto bar-section">
      <h2 class="text-title text-bark-800 mb-3 reveal">Crime Data</h2>
      <p class="text-bark-500 mb-10 max-w-2xl reveal" data-delay="100">
        Numbers first, narratives second. Bolivia's crime statistics tell a more nuanced story
        than travel advisories suggest.
      </p>

      <!-- Homicide comparison table -->
      <div class="overflow-x-auto reveal" data-delay="200">
        <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-bark-200">
          <thead class="bg-bark-800">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-display font-semibold text-[0.7rem] tracking-[0.05em] uppercase text-bark-50">Country</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-display font-semibold text-[0.7rem] tracking-[0.05em] uppercase text-bark-50">Homicide Rate</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-display font-semibold text-[0.7rem] tracking-[0.05em] uppercase text-bark-50">Context</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-b border-bark-100 bg-white">
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-bark-600">Ecuador</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-bark-800 font-semibold">~44.5/100K</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-bark-500">Surged from 5.7 in 2018; most violent in South America in 2023</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-bark-100 bg-bark-50">
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-bark-600">Colombia</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-bark-800 font-semibold">~20&ndash;30/100K</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-bark-500">Improved dramatically but still high</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-bark-100 bg-white">
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-bark-600">Mexico</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-bark-800 font-semibold">~20+/100K</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-bark-500">High aggregate, varies enormously by state</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-bark-100 bg-bark-50">
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-bark-600">United States</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-bark-800 font-semibold">~6.4/100K</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-bark-500">For comparison &mdash; higher than Bolivia</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-bark-100 bg-accent/5">
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-bark-800 font-semibold">Bolivia</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-accent font-bold text-lg">4.3/100K</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-bark-700 font-medium">Relatively low for the region (535 total homicides, 2023)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-bark-100 bg-white">
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-bark-600">Peru</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-bark-800 font-semibold">&lt;10/100K</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-bark-500">Lower end of spectrum</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="bg-bark-50">
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-bark-600">Chile</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-bark-800 font-semibold">&lt;5/100K</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-bark-500">Among the safest in the region</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p class="text-bark-400 text-xs mt-4 reveal" data-delay="300">
        Sources: <a href="https://data.worldbank.org/indicator/VC.IHR.PSRC.P5?locations=BO" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent/70 hover:text-accent underline">World Bank</a>,
        <a href="https://www.statista.com/statistics/984859/homicide-rate-bolivia/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent/70 hover:text-accent underline">Statista</a>,
        <a href="https://insightcrime.org/news/insight-crime-2024-homicide-round-up/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent/70 hover:text-accent underline">InSight Crime 2024</a>
      </p>

      <!-- Coroico specific -->
      <div class="mt-12 bg-bark-100 rounded-xl p-8 border border-bark-200 reveal" data-delay="300">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mb-3">Coroico Specifically</h3>
        <p class="text-bark-600 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed mb-4">
          <strong class="text-bark-800">No municipality-level crime statistics are publicly available for Coroico.</strong>
          Bolivia does not publish granular crime data by municipality the way Mexico or Colombia do.
          We state this honestly rather than presenting national statistics as if they apply to a specific town.
        </p>
        <p class="text-bark-600 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed mb-4">
          What we can say from available sources: Coroico is a small tourist town (~23,000 municipality population)
          frequently described as "quiet during the week" and a "weekend getaway for pacenos" (La Paz residents).
          Multiple travel sources describe it as having "extremely friendly people." It is listed among the
          "12 Best Places to Retire in Bolivia" by multiple outlets citing "ideal climate, scenic beauty,
          and low cost of living."
        </p>
        <p class="text-bark-600 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
          Petty crime exists as it does throughout Bolivia. Violent crime targeting foreigners in Coroico
          specifically has no documented pattern in available sources. La Paz city's crime indices
          (Crime Index: 60.13, Safety Index: 39.87 on Numbeo) should <strong class="text-bark-800">not</strong>
          be directly applied to Coroico &mdash; urban crime patterns are largely absent in small Yungas towns.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Travel Advisories -->
  <section class="bg-bark-100 py-24 px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto bar-section">
      <h2 class="text-title text-bark-800 mb-3 reveal">Travel Advisories</h2>
      <p class="text-bark-500 mb-10 max-w-2xl reveal" data-delay="100">
        What governments say about traveling to Bolivia, and what that means in context.
      </p>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 reveal" data-delay="200">
        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl border border-bark-200 p-8">
          <span class="text-label text-bark-400 text-[0.6rem]">United States</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mt-2 mb-3">Level 2 &mdash; Exercise Increased Caution</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">
            Due to civil unrest. This is the same level as France, Germany, and the UK.
            It is <strong class="text-bark-800">not</strong> Level 3 (Reconsider Travel) or Level 4 (Do Not Travel).
          </p>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">
            The Chapare region is specifically designated "Do Not Travel" due to violent crime.
            <strong class="text-bark-800">The Yungas is not.</strong> It falls under the general Level 2.
          </p>
          <p class="text-bark-400 text-xs">
            <a href="https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/traveladvisories/traveladvisories/bolivia-travel-advisory.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent/70 hover:text-accent underline">US State Department, June 2024</a>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl border border-bark-200 p-8">
          <span class="text-label text-bark-400 text-[0.6rem]">United Kingdom</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mt-2 mb-3">General Caution</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">
            Advises caution with cameras and binoculars in coca-growing areas including the Yungas,
            "where people can be suspicious of anyone taking photographs."
          </p>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">
            Warns about road safety on the Death Road and road conditions during rainy season.
            <strong class="text-bark-800">Does not advise against travel to Coroico or the Yungas.</strong>
          </p>
          <p class="text-bark-400 text-xs">
            <a href="https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bolivia/safety-and-security" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent/70 hover:text-accent underline">UK FCDO</a>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl border border-bark-200 p-8">
          <span class="text-label text-bark-400 text-[0.6rem]">Canada</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mt-2 mb-3">Exercise High Degree of Caution</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">
            General advisory to avoid Chapare and Yungas "due to elevated crime" linked to coca
            production. Canada's advisory is the most cautious of the three regarding the Yungas specifically.
          </p>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">
            Context matters: Canada groups the entire Yungas with the Chapare, which is a significantly
            different risk profile. The Yungas is not the Chapare.
          </p>
          <p class="text-bark-400 text-xs">
            <a href="https://travel.gc.ca/destinations/bolivia" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent/70 hover:text-accent underline">Canada Travel Advice</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Coca Economy Context -->
  <section class="py-24 px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <h2 class="text-title text-bark-800 mb-6 reveal">The Coca Economy &mdash; Context, Not Controversy</h2>
        <p class="text-bark-600 text-[1.1rem] leading-[1.85] mb-6 reveal" data-delay="100">
          The Yungas is one of Bolivia's two legal coca-growing regions. This is the primary reason
          for elevated travel advisories. Understanding the distinction between the Yungas and the
          Chapare is essential.
        </p>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-px bg-bark-200 rounded-xl overflow-hidden mb-8 reveal" data-delay="200">
          <div class="bg-bark-50 p-8">
            <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-accent mb-3">Yungas Coca</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2">
              <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">Traditional, high-quality cultivation</li>
              <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">Primarily for domestic use: chewing and tea</li>
              <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">Legal and constitutionally protected in Bolivia</li>
              <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">Centuries of cultural tradition</li>
              <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60"><strong class="text-bark-800">Not</strong> associated with international drug trade</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-bark-50 p-8">
            <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ember mb-3">Chapare Coca</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2">
              <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-ember/60">More recent, large-scale cultivation</li>
              <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-ember/60">More associated with cocaine production</li>
              <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-ember/60">Higher security force presence and conflict</li>
              <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-ember/60">US "Do Not Travel" designation</li>
              <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-ember/60">Different geographic region from Coroico</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <blockquote class="border-l-3 border-accent pl-6 py-4 bg-accent/5 rounded-r-xl reveal" data-delay="300">
          <p class="text-bark-700 font-display font-medium text-[1.1rem] leading-relaxed italic">
            Coca leaf is to cocaine as grape is to brandy. The leaf itself is mild and nutritious &mdash;
            used for millennia as a stimulant, digestive aid, and sacred offering.
          </p>
        </blockquote>

        <p class="text-bark-600 text-[1.1rem] leading-[1.85] mt-6 reveal" data-delay="400">
          <strong class="text-bark-800">BARK's position:</strong> We respect local agricultural traditions entirely.
          Coca is deeply cultural in the Yungas. Disrespecting it would mean disrespecting the community
          we are joining. BARK does not grow coca but fully supports the rights of local communities
          to continue their traditional cultivation.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Political Stability -->
  <section class="bg-bark-100 py-24 px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto bar-section">
      <h2 class="text-title text-bark-800 mb-3 reveal">Political Stability</h2>
      <p class="text-bark-500 mb-10 max-w-2xl reveal" data-delay="100">
        Bolivia's political landscape is dynamic. Anyone planning to build something permanent
        here needs to understand the patterns.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4 reveal" data-delay="200">
        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl p-8 border border-bark-200">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mb-3">Recent History</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Bolivia has experienced significant political instability: the 2019 crisis following
            Evo Morales' resignation, the 2020 interim government, and the 2024 economic and
            political tensions. In August 2025, Bolivia elected a pro-market, pro-reform government
            that is seeking to restore international relations and pursue investor-friendly reforms.
            The trajectory is toward stability, but Bolivia's political culture is cyclical.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl p-8 border border-bark-200">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mb-3">Road Blockades (Bloqueos)</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Road blockades are a deeply embedded Bolivian protest tradition. The La Paz&ndash;Coroico
            route gets blocked during national disputes. During the 2024 political crisis, blockades
            disrupted travel and supply chains across the country. Tourism took "a serious hit."
            <strong class="text-bark-800">This is a real planning consideration, not an edge case.</strong>
            Blockades can cut supplies for days. Any community in the Yungas needs a plan for this.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl p-8 border border-bark-200">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mb-3">Economic Context</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Bolivia is experiencing a prolonged economic crisis: severe fuel shortages, dollar scarcity,
            and inflation exceeding 20% as of 2025 (IMF). Foreign reserves have dropped to approximately
            $100M. The cooperative sector is constitutionally recognized and generally receives favorable
            treatment, but the broader economic environment is challenging. Foreign investment protections
            exist but are weaker than in neighboring countries &mdash; Bolivia abrogated its bilateral
            investment treaty with the US in 2012.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Natural Hazards -->
  <section class="py-24 px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto bar-section">
      <h2 class="text-title text-bark-800 mb-3 reveal">Natural Hazards</h2>
      <p class="text-bark-500 mb-10 max-w-2xl reveal" data-delay="100">
        The Yungas is beautiful because of the same geography that creates these hazards.
        Understanding them is the first step to managing them.
      </p>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 reveal" data-delay="200">
        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl border border-bark-200 p-8 border-l-4 border-l-ember">
          <span class="text-label text-ember text-[0.6rem]">Primary hazard</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mt-2 mb-3">Landslides</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            This is the number one natural hazard. The rainy season (November&ndash;March) saturates the steep
            Yungas slopes, causing frequent landslides. The old "Death Road" earned its name primarily from these.
            Road closures happen multiple times per rainy season and can last hours to days. BARK's site
            selection and building standards must account for slope stability and drainage.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl border border-bark-200 p-8">
          <span class="text-label text-bark-400 text-[0.6rem]">Seasonal</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mt-2 mb-3">Road Closures</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Related to landslides but worth its own entry. The La Paz&ndash;Coroico road (the "new road"
            opened in 2006/2007 to replace the Death Road) is significantly safer but still subject to
            closures from mudslides and rockfall during heavy rains. During closures, Coroico is
            effectively isolated from La Paz.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl border border-bark-200 p-8">
          <span class="text-label text-bark-400 text-[0.6rem]">Seasonal</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mt-2 mb-3">Flooding</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            River flooding in lower valleys during heavy rains. Coroico town itself is elevated
            enough to avoid most flooding, but low-lying agricultural areas and roads near rivers
            are vulnerable. Site selection should account for flood plains and drainage patterns.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl border border-bark-200 p-8">
          <span class="text-label text-bark-400 text-[0.6rem]">Low risk</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mt-2 mb-3">Earthquakes</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Bolivia has moderate seismic activity. The Yungas is not in the highest-risk zone
            (that would be the western volcanic chain), but earthquakes can occur. Building
            standards should include basic seismic resilience without requiring full earthquake-proof
            construction.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl border border-bark-200 p-8 md:col-span-2">
          <span class="text-label text-bark-400 text-[0.6rem]">Daily</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mt-2 mb-3">UV Radiation</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Strong UV at 1,750m elevation with thin, clear mountain air. Not a dramatic hazard,
            but chronic exposure without protection causes real skin damage. Sunscreen, hats,
            and UV-protective clothing are daily essentials for outdoor work. This is especially
            important for people with lighter skin who are accustomed to lower elevations.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BARK Security Measures -->
  <section class="bg-bark-100 bg-warm-gradient py-24 px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-title text-bark-800 mb-3 reveal">BARK Security Measures</h2>
      <p class="text-bark-500 mb-10 max-w-2xl reveal" data-delay="100">
        How BARK plans to address the realities described above. These are design decisions,
        not aspirations.
      </p>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-px bg-bark-200 rounded-xl overflow-hidden reveal" data-delay="200">
        <div class="bg-bark-50 p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 text-sm mb-3">Food Reserves</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            On-site food production supplemented by stored reserves. During road blockades,
            the community can sustain itself independently for weeks. This is not optional &mdash;
            it is a core infrastructure requirement.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bark-50 p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 text-sm mb-3">Water Independence</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Independent water collection, filtration, and storage systems. No dependency on
            municipal water supply. The Yungas receives 1,100&ndash;1,300mm of annual rainfall &mdash;
            water scarcity is not the issue. Water quality and storage are.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bark-50 p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 text-sm mb-3">Solar Power</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Off-grid solar micro-grid with battery storage. No dependency on the national
            electricity grid. Power independence means lights, communications, and medical
            equipment function regardless of external conditions.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bark-50 p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 text-sm mb-3">Satellite Communications</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Starlink for internet, satellite phone for emergencies. Mesh network communication
            independent of cell towers. When roads are blocked and cell towers go down,
            BARK maintains contact with the outside world.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bark-50 p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 text-sm mb-3">Community Watch</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Community-based security awareness. Good relationships with neighbors and local
            authorities. The best security is a community where everyone knows everyone and
            looks out for each other &mdash; supplemented by practical protocols.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bark-50 p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 text-sm mb-3">Emergency Protocols</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Written emergency protocols for medical evacuation, natural disasters, road closure,
            and political unrest. Dedicated vehicle maintained for emergency transport. First aid
            station staffed by the community health worker. Regular drills.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
